--- !u!114 &114654652813765854
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1007513189690300}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b92691faec7c95e2b99a1e9aebad607, type: 3}
  m_Name:
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.32941177, g: 0.22745098, b: 0.21176471, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: cc6284d09f458b845b1fde322281907e, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 22
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 2
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "1. Registration\nAlliance Leaders or R4 officers or higher of alliances in the Alliance Power Leaderboard top <color=#f43b3b>20</color> can register for the event. New Alliance members to join <color=#f43b3b>after the registration has ended</color> cannot participate, <color=#f43b3b>nor earn</color> alliance participation rewards. Each Alliance can sign up two Legions. The participants’ list will be locked as well and cannot be changed afterward.\nRequest for battle: R4 officers or lower can only register for any one of the legion, but they can freely switch between the two before registration ends.\n\n2. Combatants\nUp to 30 combatants and 10 substitutes will be determined by the Alliance Leader and R4 officers. <color=#f43b3b>Each member can only be selected for one Legion, either as a substitute or as a combatant</color>.\n\n3. Matchmaking\nLegions are matched based on their Matchmaking Points and win rates.\nMatchmaking Points are determined by the Soldier Power of the top 25 registered Governors.\nThe main sources of Soldier Power are Governor Gear, Hero Gear, and Battle Tech Power.\nLegions will first be matched with other registrant selecting the same time slot. If no match can be found, it they will then match with legions registering for different time slot. The final time slot will be randomly picked in-between the two selected time slot.\n\n4. Enter Battlefield\nParticipating Governors can enter the battlefield once the battle begins provided they have no squads currently scouting or marching outside the Town, no injured soldiers in their Infirmary, no burning Guard Station, and no reinforcements from other Governors in their Embassy.\n\n5. Commencement\nOnce on the battlefield, <color=#2c9df4>our forces will be tagged blue</color> and <color=#f43b3b>enemies red</color>.\n\n6. Battle Phases\nPhase 1: Sanctums, Abbeys, Belltowers, and the Royal Stables can be contested.\nPhase 2: the Swordshrine, Hall of Reformation, and the Mercenary Camp can be contested.\nPhase 3: Undercellars will start to appear randomly over the map.\n\nWhichever side has accumulated the most [Alliance Relic Points] by the end of the battle will be declared the winner."
  m_PointerTween: 0
  m_TweenScale: {x: 1.2, y: 1.2}
  m_isMaxWidth: 0
  m_maxWidth: 0
  colorType: 0
  m_isStatic: 1
  m_key: arsenalwar_ui_115
  supportHyperLink: 0
